WEBVTT

00:00:01.682 --> 00:00:02.187
GOOD AFTERNOON, CLASS.

00:00:02.231 --> 00:00:04.885
Class: GOOD AFTERNOON,
MADAME HOOCH.

00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:06.713
GOOD AFTERNOON, AMANDA.
GOOD AFTERNOON.

00:00:08.628 --> 00:00:11.196
WELCOME TO YOUR FIRST
FLYING LESSON.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.068
WELL, WHAT ARE YOU
WAITING FOR?

00:00:13.111 --> 00:00:15.548
EVERYONE STEP UP TO THE LEFT
SIDE OF THEIR BROOMSTICK.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:18.377
COME ON NOW.
HURRY UP.

00:00:18.421 --> 00:00:20.031
STICK YOUR RIGHT HAND
OVER THE BROOM

00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:21.554
AND SAY, "UP."

00:00:21.598 --> 00:00:23.687
Class: UP! UP!

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.688
UP.

00:00:24.731 --> 00:00:25.863
WOW.

00:00:25.906 --> 00:00:26.864
UP.

00:00:26.907 --> 00:00:29.475
UP! UP! UP!

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:31.260
UP! UP!

00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:32.304
WITH FEELING!

00:00:32.348 --> 00:00:34.654
UP!
UP!

00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:36.613
UP! UP.

00:00:36.656 --> 00:00:39.006
UP. UP. UP.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.356
UP!

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:41.487
OH!

00:00:41.531 --> 00:00:44.273
SHUT UP, HARRY.

00:00:44.316 --> 00:00:47.319
NOW, ONCE YOU'VE GOT
HOLD OF YOUR BROOM,

00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:50.627
I WANT YOU TO MOUNT IT
AND GRIP IT TIGHT.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.325
YOU DON'T WANT TO BE
SLIDING OFF THE END.

00:00:53.369 --> 00:00:56.154
WHEN I BLOW MY WHISTLE,
I WANT EACH OF YOU

00:00:56.198 --> 00:00:58.852
TO KICK OFF
FROM THE GROUND HARD.

00:00:58.896 --> 00:01:02.726
KEEP YOUR BROOMS STEADY,
HOVER FOR A MOMENT,

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:06.773
THEN LEAN FORWARD SLIGHTLY
AND TOUCH BACK DOWN.

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:08.384
ON MY WHISTLE--

00:01:08.427 --> 00:01:10.037
3, 2...

00:01:10.081 --> 00:01:11.474
[FWEET]

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:12.649
OH...

00:01:12.692 --> 00:01:14.346
Hooch:
MR. LONGBOTTOM.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.826
NEVILLE,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:17.784
WE'RE NOT SUPPOSED
TO TAKE OFF YET.

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:18.872
AAH!

00:01:18.916 --> 00:01:21.875
M-M-MR. LONG--
MR. LONGBOTTOM!

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:23.355
CAREFUL, NEVILLE!

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:25.836
WHOA!

00:01:25.879 --> 00:01:26.967
HELP!

00:01:27.011 --> 00:01:28.578
COME BACK DOWN
THIS INSTANT!

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.623
[SCREAMING]

00:01:32.973 --> 00:01:34.975
[GRUNTING]

00:01:36.977 --> 00:01:38.196
HELP!

00:01:39.502 --> 00:01:40.807
MR. LONGBOTTOM!

00:01:41.982 --> 00:01:42.983
AAH!

00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:46.117
WHOA!

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:47.684
AAH!

00:01:49.903 --> 00:01:51.992
[SHOUTING]
HELP!

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:55.170
[GRUNTS]

00:01:58.173 --> 00:01:59.130
OW!

00:01:59.174 --> 00:02:01.176
EVERYONE OUT OF THE WAY!

00:02:05.702 --> 00:02:07.573
Hooch: COME ON, GET UP.

00:02:07.617 --> 00:02:08.574
OW! OW!

00:02:08.618 --> 00:02:10.141
OH, OH, OH, OH, DEAR.

00:02:10.185 --> 00:02:11.273
IT'S A BROKEN WRIST.

00:02:11.316 --> 00:02:13.231
TCH, TCH, TCH.
GOOD BOY. COME ON NOW.

00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:14.885
UP YOU GET.

00:02:16.103 --> 00:02:18.323
EVERYONE'S TO KEEP THEIR FEET
FIRMLY ON THE GROUND

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.934
WHILE I TAKE MR. LONGBOTTOM
TO THE HOSPITAL WING.

00:02:20.978 --> 00:02:22.371
UNDERSTAND?

00:02:22.414 --> 00:02:24.634
IF I SEE A SINGLE
BROOM IN THE AIR,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.245
THE ONE RIDING IT WILL FIND
THEMSELVES OUT OF HOGWARTS

00:02:27.289 --> 00:02:29.160
BEFORE THEY CAN
SAY "QUIDDITCH."

00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:30.248
[LAUGHS]

00:02:30.292 --> 00:02:31.771
DID YOU SEE HIS FACE?

00:02:31.815 --> 00:02:34.252
MAYBE IF THE FAT LUMP
HAD GIVEN THIS A SQUEEZE,

00:02:34.296 --> 00:02:36.646
HE WOULD HAVE REMEMBERED
TO FALL ON HIS FAT ASS.

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.300
GIVE IT HERE, MALFOY.

00:02:39.997 --> 00:02:40.998
NO.

00:02:41.041 --> 00:02:41.999
I THINK I'LL
LEAVE IT SOMEWHERE

00:02:42.042 --> 00:02:43.653
FOR LONGBOTTOM
TO FIND.

00:02:47.526 --> 00:02:49.485
HOW 'BOUT ON THE ROOF?

00:02:50.877 --> 00:02:52.705
WHAT'S THE MATTER, POTTER?

00:02:52.749 --> 00:02:55.317
A BIT BEYOND YOUR REACH?

00:02:57.493 --> 00:02:59.321
HARRY, NO WAY.

00:02:59.364 --> 00:03:00.974
YOU HEARD WHAT
MADAME HOOCH SAID.

00:03:01.018 --> 00:03:03.629
BESIDES, YOU DON'T
EVEN KNOW HOW TO FLY.

00:03:05.109 --> 00:03:07.024
WHAT AN IDIOT.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:11.420
GIVE IT HERE,
MALFOY,

00:03:11.463 --> 00:03:13.160
OR I'LL KNOCK YOU
OFF YOUR BROOM!

00:03:13.204 --> 00:03:15.206
IS THAT SO?

00:03:18.557 --> 00:03:21.560
HAVE IT YOUR WAY, THEN.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.674
[ALL CHEERING]

00:03:51.547 --> 00:03:54.027
THAT WAS WICKED!

00:03:54.071 --> 00:03:55.333
GOOD JOB, HARRY.

00:03:55.377 --> 00:03:57.901
OH, THAT WAS
WICKED, HARRY.

00:03:57.944 --> 00:03:59.119
HARRY POTTER?

00:04:00.643 --> 00:04:02.297
FOLLOW ME.

00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:07.084
[LAUGHS]

00:04:11.393 --> 00:04:15.048
Quirrell: AN IGUANA
SUCH AS THIS IS AN...

00:04:15.092 --> 00:04:16.223
YOU WAIT HERE.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:19.009
ESSENTIAL
INGREDIENT IN...

00:04:19.052 --> 00:04:20.837
PROFESSOR QUIRRELL,
EXCUSE ME, EXCUSE ME.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.361
COULD I BORROW WOOD
FOR A MOMENT, PLEASE?

00:04:23.405 --> 00:04:26.277
OH, Y-YES.
OF COURSE.

00:04:26.321 --> 00:04:29.236
[EERIE ROARING]

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.717
Quirrell:
THE VAMPIRE BAT...

00:04:31.761 --> 00:04:33.763
POTTER, THIS IS
OLIVER WOOD.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:37.680
WOOD, I HAVE
FOUND YOU A SEEKER.

00:04:39.595 --> 00:04:40.813
HAVE YOU HEARD?

00:04:40.857 --> 00:04:43.555
HARRY POTTER'S
THE NEW GRYFFINDOR SEEKER.

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:45.731
I ALWAYS KNEW
HE'D DO WELL.

00:04:45.775 --> 00:04:47.385
SEEKER?

00:04:47.429 --> 00:04:50.301
BUT FIRST YEARS NEVER
MAKE THE HOUSE TEAMS.

00:04:50.345 --> 00:04:52.782
YOU MUST BE THE YOUNGEST
QUIDDITCH PLAYER...

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.871
IN A CENTURY,
ACCORDING TO McGONAGALL.

00:04:54.914 --> 00:04:57.700
HEY, WELL DONE, HARRY.
WOOD'S JUST TOLD US.

00:04:57.743 --> 00:04:59.441
FRED AND GEORGE ARE
ON THE TEAM, TOO...

00:04:59.484 --> 00:05:00.964
BEATERS.

00:05:01.007 --> 00:05:02.792
OUR JOB IS TO MAKE
SURE THAT YOU

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.576
DON'T GET BLOODIED
UP TOO BAD.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.969
CAN'T MAKE ANY
PROMISES, OF COURSE.

00:05:06.012 --> 00:05:07.449
ROUGH GAME,
QUIDDITCH.

00:05:07.492 --> 00:05:09.973
BRUTAL. BUT NO ONE'S
DIED IN YEARS.

00:05:10.016 --> 00:05:11.453
SOMEONE WILL VANISH
OCCASIONALLY...

00:05:11.496 --> 00:05:14.107
BUT THEY'LL TURN UP
IN A MONTH OR 2!

00:05:14.151 --> 00:05:15.718
OH, GO ON, HARRY.

00:05:15.761 --> 00:05:17.807
QUIDDITCH IS GREAT.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.156
BEST GAME THERE IS.

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:20.462
AND YOU'LL
BE GREAT, TOO.

00:05:20.505 --> 00:05:22.507
BUT I'VE NEVER EVEN
PLAYED QUIDDITCH.

00:05:22.551 --> 00:05:24.117
WHAT IF I MAKE
A FOOL OF MYSELF?

00:05:24.161 --> 00:05:26.119
YOU WON'T MAKE
A FOOL OF YOURSELF.

00:05:26.163 --> 00:05:27.469
IT'S IN YOUR BLOOD.

00:05:34.301 --> 00:05:35.694
WHOA.

00:05:35.738 --> 00:05:38.654
HARRY, YOU NEVER
TOLD ME YOUR FATHER

00:05:38.697 --> 00:05:40.090
WAS A SEEKER, TOO.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:43.398
I...DIDN'T KNOW.

00:05:48.925 --> 00:05:49.654
I'M TELLING YOU,
IT'S SPOOKY.

